# ── Zupersync ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Receives Zuper webhooks and keeps the shared Supabase (the one JMS/Tuper uses)
# live. There are no mirror tables: this service writes the jms.* tables that
# every app already reads.

PORT=3020
NODE_ENV=production

# ── Supabase (the SAME project JMS connects to) ──────────────────────────────
# The service role key is required: this service writes across the jms schema
# and must bypass RLS, exactly as the migration CLI already does.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
DEFAULT_TENANT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

# ── Zuper API ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A webhook is only a trigger; the record is always re-fetched from Zuper, which
# stays the system of record. Also used to push app-side changes back.
#
# BASE ONLY — do NOT end this with "/api". Request paths already start with
# "/api/", and the two are concatenated, so a trailing "/api" builds
# ".../api/api/jobs/{uid}". Zuper answers that with a 404 and an HTML body, so it
# fails as a JSON parse error rather than as an obvious misconfiguration.
# (config.ts strips it and warns, but set it correctly.)
# The plain and "eks-" hostnames serve the same API; this is the one the database's
# zuper_sync_config.api_base uses, which is what the sync engine actually reads.
ZUPER_API_URL=https://eks-ap-south-1.zuperpro.com
ZUPER_API_KEY=

# ── Inbound webhook authentication ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Zuper has no "secret" field — each webhook carries ONE custom header you
# define (its form is literally `key` / `value`). Set the same pair here and in
# every Zuper webhook. Deliveries that don't match are stored for forensics and
# NOT processed.
ZUPER_WEBHOOK_HEADER=x-zupersync-key
ZUPER_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ── Replay ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Zuper retries a webhook three times and then gives up; everything after that is
# ours. Deliveries that were stored but never finished (a restart mid-processing,
# a transient Zuper 500) are retried on this interval.
#
# Attempts are capped: a delivery that can never succeed - its record was deleted
# in Zuper, or it names an entity Zuper has no by-uid read for - stops retrying
# and stays visible in the dashboard with its error, rather than consuming the
# 200-700 req/min API budget forever.
RECONCILE_ENABLED=true
RECONCILE_REPLAY_SECONDS=120
RECONCILE_REPLAY_BATCH=25
RECONCILE_MAX_ATTEMPTS=5

# ── Window sweep — NOT IMPLEMENTED ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Re-reading every job Zuper changed in a rolling window is the only thing that
# catches a delivery that never arrived AT ALL, which is what a long outage
# produces. These values record the intent; no code reads them yet. Until it is
# built, a delivery Zuper abandoned after its three tries is lost.
RECONCILE_NEAR_DAYS_BACK=1
RECONCILE_NEAR_DAYS_AHEAD=21
